        "tag": "title",
        "text": "79"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 426.5,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Academic writing: making sense"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 407.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Presenting arguments and commenting on others’ work"
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 465.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If you advocate something, you argue in favour of it: He advocated capital punishment."
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If you deduce something, you reach a conclusion by thinking carefully about the known facts: Look"
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 425.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "at these sentences and see if you can deduce how the imperfect tense is used."
      },
      {
        "y": 124,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 486.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If you infer something, you reach a conclusion indirectly: From contemporary accounts of his"
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 434.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "research, we can infer that results were slower to come than he had anticipated."
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If someone’s work complements someone else’s, it combines well with it so that each piece of work"
      },
      {
        "y": 160,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 467.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "becomes more effective: Elswick’s (2016) research complements that of Johnson (2012)."
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 481.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If someone’s work overlaps with someone else’s work, it partially covers the same material."
      },
      {
        "y": 184,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You might call someone’s work: empirical [based on what is observed rather than theory], ambiguous"
      },
      {
        "y": 196,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 495.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[open to different interpretations], coherent [logically structured], comprehensive [covering all that is"
      },
      {
        "y": 208,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 283.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "relevant], authoritative [thorough and expert]."
      },
      {
        "y": 229.3,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 296.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Talking about figures and processes"
      },
      {
        "y": 246.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 497.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If figures are referred to as arbitrary, they are based on chance or personal choice rather than a"
      },
      {
        "y": 259.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 245.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "system or data that supports them."
      },
      {
        "y": 270.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 391,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Figures that deviate from the norm are different from what is typical."
      },
      {
        "y": 282.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 345.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If statistics distort the picture, they give a false impression."
      },
      {
        "y": 294.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If you refer to the incidence of something, e.g. a disease, you are talking about how often it occurs."
      },
      {
        "y": 306.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 474.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If something, e.g. the incidence of brown eyes, is predominant, it is the largest in number."
      },
      {
        "y": 318.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 468.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If things, e.g. stages in a process, happen in sequence, they happen in a particular order."
      },
      {
        "y": 331.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 519.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If you want to say that something happens in many places or with many people, you can say that it is"
      },
      {
        "y": 342.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 399.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "widespread, e.g. widespread outbreaks of an illness, widespread alarm."
      },
      {
        "y": 364.2,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 331.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Words typically used in academic contexts"
      },
