      {
        "y": 68.6,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "79.1"
      },
      {
        "y": 71.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 393.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Which of the five verbs in A opposite best fits in each sentence?"
      },
      {
        "y": 87.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 516.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 The French and Swedish teams work in similar areas, but their research, fortunately, does not"
      },
      {
        "y": 99.8,
        "x0": 186.5,
        "x1": 472.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": ". However, the French data the Swedish data very well."
      },
      {
        "y": 111.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 527.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 Look at the complete set of graphs and see if you can the rules governing the data"
      },
      {
        "y": 123.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 174.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from them."
      },
      {
        "y": 135.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 387,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 This article a different approach to the problem."
      },
      {
        "y": 147.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 483.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 A great deal can be about the artist’s state of mind from his later works."
      },
      {
        "y": 163.9,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "79.2"
      },
      {
        "y": 166.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 416,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Which of the five adjectives in A best describes each of these things?"
      },
      {
        "y": 183.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 398.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 a textbook written by the most highly regarded expert in the field"
      },
      {
        "y": 195.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 315.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 research based on a survey of the population"
      },
      {
        "y": 207.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 380.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 a poem which can be understood in two quite different ways"
      },
      {
        "y": 219.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 360.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 an argument which is well-expressed and easy to follow"
      },
      {
        "y": 231.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 389.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 a textbook which gives a broad overview of an entire discipline"
      },
      {
        "y": 247.2,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "79.3"
      },
      {
        "y": 249.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 394.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Answer these questions which use vocabulary from B opposite."
      },
      {
        "y": 266.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 538,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 If the incidence of asthma in children is increasing, what is actually going up: (a) the seriousness of"
      },
      {
        "y": 278.5,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 362.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "asthma attacks or (b) the number of asthmatic children?"
      },
      {
        "y": 290.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 405.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 What are the next two numbers in this sequence: 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36?"
      },
      {
        "y": 302.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 503.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 If the average mark in a maths test was 68% and Ulla’s mark deviated noticeably from that"
      },
      {
        "y": 314.5,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 318.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "average, what do we know about Ulla’s mark?"
      },
      {
        "y": 326.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 524.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 If facts are distorted, are they presented (a) accurately, (b) clearly or (c) in a misleading fashion?"
      },
      {
        "y": 338.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 536.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 If sociologists choose the subjects of their research in an arbitrary fashion, do they take care to get"
      },
      {
        "y": 350.5,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 349.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "people from an appropriate balance of backgrounds?"
      },
      {
        "y": 366.6,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "79.4"
      },
      {
        "y": 369.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 479,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Use items from C to rewrite the underlined parts of the sentences in a more formal"
      },
      {
        "y": 381.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 184.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "academic style."
      },
      {
        "y": 397.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 410.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 The information lies in archives that must not be opened until 2050."
      },
      {
        "y": 409.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 332.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 He thought up his theory while still a young man."
      },
      {
        "y": 421.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 398,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 Each of the symbols in the phonetic alphabet stands for a sound."
      },
      {
        "y": 433.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 502.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 This study went against what was previously held to be true, and so started a great deal of"
      },
      {
        "y": 445.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 305,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "discussion amongst specialists in the field."
      },
      {
        "y": 457.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 408.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 Details of the experiment have been added at the end of the report."
      },
      {
        "y": 469.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 523.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 Jelowski’s book thinks about the rise and fall of great Empires over two millennia. She sees the"
      },
      {
        "y": 481.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 527.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Roman Empire as an example of a pattern that has repeated itself in other times and other parts"
      },
      {
        "y": 493.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 180.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of the world."
      },
      {
        "y": 509.9,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "79.5"
      },
      {
        "y": 512.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 508.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Rewrite this paragraph. Change the bold words and use words from C opposite to make it"
      },
      {
        "y": 524.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 215.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "sound more academic."
      },
      {
        "y": 570.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 504.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The present study was initially thought up in order to"
      },
      {
        "y": 582.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 497.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "validate a new method of enquiry by which genetic"
      },
      {
        "y": 594.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 511.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "information could be used to predict disease. The study"
      },
      {
        "y": 606.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 513.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "goes against the findings of Hill (2009); indeed it would"
      },
      {
        "y": 618.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 497.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "appear to show the opposite of what he claimed. It"
      },
      {
        "y": 630.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 503.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "presents a rather different view of the genetic factors"
      },
      {
        "y": 642.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 505.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "which cause disease. Despite this, the study does not"
      },
      {
        "y": 654.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 514.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "wipe out Hill’s, as his studies served the very important"
      },
      {
        "y": 666.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 486.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "purpose of devising symbols to stand for certain"
      },
      {
        "y": 678.7,
        "x0": 303.8,
        "x1": 496.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "tendencies, in this way facilitating further research."
      }
    ],
